// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
; specs/widgets/fasm-skyline.t27 -- a 7-series FASM file drawn as a skyline on the XC7A200T die
; Source of truth for public/widgets/fasm-skyline/ (gHashTag/trinity, apps/website):
; scripts/widget-pages-from-spec.mjs compiles this file, checks its constants, evaluates the tests
; below and writes the page; the page hands every constant to tool.js as window.T27_WIDGET.
; tool.js holds no English of its own: every word on screen is a SAY_ constant here, every number
; the tool relies on is a K_ constant or a field of the two data files named below.
; ASCII only (L3), English only (LANG-EN).

; WHAT IT DOES: the reader drops a 7-series .fasm (the text nextpnr-xilinx writes with --fasm). The
; page counts the features each tile sets, one FASM line being one feature, the tile being the
; text before the first '.', and draws the die isometrically: the floor is every tile of the
; XC7A200T's 265 x 261 grid coloured by family, and each touched tile is a column whose height is
; its feature count. It shows the tiles touched, the features set, the tallest tile and the share
; of the die's configurable tiles touched, a table by family, and the tile under the pointer. The
; reader can rotate, pan and zoom, and download the skyline as a PNG and as an STL. The file is
; read with FileReader and sent nowhere.

; HOW IT COUNTS (public/widgets/fasm-skyline/skyline.js, run by the page and by the data script):
; '#' comments and '{...}' annotations are dropped; a line whose value is zero (a BRAM INIT word of
; all zeros, for example) sets no bit and is counted apart, not as a feature; a 64-bit LUT INIT is
; one feature, not 64. A tile name places itself only if prjxray-db has a tile of that type at the
; grid cell the name maps to; every other name is listed as not drawn, never guessed at.

; DATA PROVENANCE: grid.json and samples.json are written by scripts/widget-data/fasm-skyline.mjs
; build, and its check job re-counts both FASM files with skyline.js and compares every K_ number
; below. grid.json is derived from prjxray-db ab1fc60 artix7/xc7a200t/tilegrid.json (sha256 in
; K_TILEGRID_SHA256); before writing it the script looks up all 69165 tiles through skyline.js and
; each must land on its own grid_x and grid_y. Sample one, node.fasm, is the TRI-NET node v2
; (hand-written Verilog) placed and routed for the ALINX AX7203 board, part xc7a200tfbg484-2: the
; same XC7A200T die as the bench's QMTech Wukong V1, a different package and board. Sample two,
; routed.fasm, is StreamTernaryMac generated from the t27 spec specs/ternary/stream_ternary_mac.t27
; and placed and routed for xc7a200tfbg676-1 by the build-receipt widget's run of 2026-10-04 (its
; receipt.json records the commands and this file's sha256). No new build was run for this widget.

; WHAT IT DOES NOT CLAIM: that either design was programmed into a board here or met timing. A
; feature count is not a bit count and not a resource count: an INT tile with 100 pips and a CLB
; tile with 100 features are not the same amount of logic. The drawing is the XC7A200T's: a file
; for another part is drawn only where its tile names are tiles of the 200T. The link-preview card
; shows sample one; a static page cannot put the reader's own skyline into a link preview, so the
; page offers the PNG to attach instead.
; phi^2 + 1/phi^2 = 3 | TRINITY

